2228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 1412 0 R
/T (APPLICATION When and where can I use it? Use this routine with any kind of visual art that stays still in time, such as painting or sculpture. You can also use the routine with non-art objects, such as a microscope, an animal skeleton, or a plant. The Elaboration Game is an especially good way to launch a writing activity because it helps students develop a detailed descriptive vocabulary. )
/E (APPLICATION When and where can I use it? Use this routine with any kind of visual art that stays still in time, such as painting or sculpture. You can also use the routine with non-art objects, such as a microscope, an animal skeleton, or a plant. The Elaboration Game is an especially good way to launch a writing activity because it helps students develop a detailed descriptive vocabulary. )
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
2229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 1412 0 R
/T (LAUNCH What are some tips for starting and using this routine? This is a great routine to launch a collaborative conversation about an artwork or object. With an object or sculpture you can ask students to view it from different sides or viewpoints. With an artwork or twodimensional piece, students have the opportunity to tackle smaller sections at a time. You could use a viewfinder or have the students use their hands to create a viewfinder to focus in on their section.)
/E (LAUNCH What are some tips for starting and using this routine? This is a great routine to launch a collaborative conversation about an artwork or object. With an object or sculpture you can ask students to view it from different sides or viewpoints. With an artwork or twodimensional piece, students have the opportunity to tackle smaller sections at a time. You could use a viewfinder or have the students use their hands to create a viewfinder to focus in on their section.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
