2630 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 8447 0 R
/T (To identify prominent and hidden qualities. Ask students, What layer immediately speaks to you? What makes you say that? Which layers seem more distant? What makes you say that? )
/E (To identify prominent and hidden qualities. Ask students, What layer immediately speaks to you? What makes you say that? Which layers seem more distant? What makes you say that? )
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
2631 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 8448 0 R
/T (To compare and contrast. Ask students to contrast two works to see how they relate to one another: Where do you see connections as well as differences in terms of the layers? )
/E (To compare and contrast. Ask students to contrast two works to see how they relate to one another: Where do you see connections as well as differences in terms of the layers? )
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
2632 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 8449 0 R
/T (To consider an individual element from one or more of the layers. Ask students to pick one of the four elements from one or more of the five layers to explore the work. )
/E (To consider an individual element from one or more of the layers. Ask students to pick one of the four elements from one or more of the five layers to explore the work. )
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
2633 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 8450 0 R
/T (To develop questions. Ask students to use the layers and their elements to develop questions they want to ask an expert about the work of art.)
/E (To develop questions. Ask students to use the layers and their elements to develop questions they want to ask an expert about the work of art.)
/Pg 62 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
