2938 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1449 0 R
/E (Systems are made up of subsystems, and are themselves parts of broader systems. In order to avoid going down the rabbit hole of everything is connected to everything, it may be helpful to encourage students to define the boundaries of their system. For example, if you are exploring the system of making an apple pie, you might limit it one particular pie; if you are exploring a recycling system, you might limit it to a geographical area.)
/Pg 79 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
