2967 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1450 0 R
/E (This routine encourages learners to slow down and look closely at a system. It helps them notice that there are different people who participate in the system and that they participate in different ways. It also encourages students to explore how one change in a system can impact the rest of the system. This thinking routine can help foster curiosity as children notice details, ask questions, make connections, and identify topics for future inquiry. It also helps children practice systems thinking.)
/Pg 80 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
