<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1479 0 R
/E (This routine can assist students of all ages to consider dichotomies that are commonly present in everyday life. Same and different are constant puzzles. Different countries have different currencies, different homes, schools and languages, yet they all share the same or similar purposes. Words can sound exactly the same as another, yet be spelled quite differently, and have very different meanings. People can be grouped together or separated because of one or more of the following: religion, skin color, education, socio-economic status, background, country of birth, etc.)
/Pg 109 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
