/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1482 0 R
/E (It works well toward the beginning of a topic of study because it begins by drawing on visual information students can readily see, and thus tends to be immediately engaging. Also, using the routine early in a topic of study encourages students to frame their learning as transfer-oriented from the outset. That said, the routine is a variation of the Visible Thinking routine, See | Wonder | Connect, which is a highly versatile routine that can be used at virtually any point in a learning trajectory.)
/Pg 112 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
