4227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 9087 0 R
/E (Once students portray a person in their system in one way, ask them how they might portray the same person in an entirely different way. This will prompt your students to understand that even within particular groups of people, there is no one perspective, but rather an array of perspectives that different and unique people may hold.)
/Pg 144 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
4228 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 9088 0 R
/E (Learners should be encouraged to consider how what people think, feel, and care about may be in alignment within a particular system, or misaligned. When misalignments emerge, ask your students how these tensions are dealt with or negotiated within the system? Discussions about unequal power structures within a system may arise.)
/Pg 144 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
