/P 1543 0 R
/T (LAUNCH What are some tips for starting and using this routine? 1. Set up. Introduce the source material and invite students to examine it carefully. This could be done individually or in pairs. This slow looking \(Tishman 2017\) shouldn't be rushed, and students should be explicitly encouraged to take time to notice things that aren't immediately apparent.)
/E (LAUNCH What are some tips for starting and using this routine? 1. Set up. Introduce the source material and invite students to examine it carefully. This could be done individually or in pairs. This slow looking \(Tishman 2017\) shouldn't be rushed, and students should be explicitly encouraged to take time to notice things that aren't immediately apparent.)
/Pg 173 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
4803 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
